Description: Read an X11 window's _NET_WM_STATE when it maps
 XWaylandSurface::map() queued a read of _NET_WM_STATE but never called
 the returned cookie, so the reply handler never ran and the window's
 initial state was ignored. X11 windows that map fullscreen or maximized,
 such as Wine/Proton games, were shown restored at their small pre-map
 size (a 314x208 Unity game window at the bottom of the screen) until
 they asked again later.
Author: Umoja developers
Forwarded: not yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-09
---
--- a/src/server/frontend_xwayland/xwayland_surface.cpp
+++ b/src/server/frontend_xwayland/xwayland_surface.cpp
@@ -476,6 +476,10 @@
                 }
             }
         });
+    // Wait for the reply and run the handler: without this the initial
+    // state was never read, so X11 windows that map fullscreen or maximized
+    // (Wine/Proton games) were shown restored at their small pre-map size.
+    cookie();
 
     // If we had more properties to read we would queue them all up before completing the first one
     uint32_t const workspace = 1;
